# Inslogic PLA Pro — Prusa MK3S+, 0.8 nozzle
# Built from the Inslogic PLA Pro Technical Data Sheet (rev. 12.02.2024),
# archived at ../../reference/inslogic_pla_pro_tds.pdf.
# The TDS lists no 0.8 mm nozzle. This profile exists because that is how this
# printer is often run here, not because Inslogic supports it.
inherits = Generic PLA @0.8 nozzle
filament_vendor = Inslogic
filament_type = PLA
filament_diameter = 1.75
filament_density = 1.20
filament_cost = 59
filament_spool_weight = 1000
temperature = 220
first_layer_temperature = 220
bed_temperature = 60
first_layer_bed_temperature = 60
filament_notes = "Inslogic PLA Pro at 0.8 nozzle - TDS rev. 12.02.2024.\n\nGRADE: the plain PLA Pro grade - product 'PLA Pro Inslogic 1KG', 59 ILS at filamentcenter.co.il (checked 29 Aug 2026). Not Matte, Silk, High-Speed, Nebulux, LW-PLA or WoodFill, which are separate products with their own sheets.\n\nVENDOR SPEC:\nDiameter 1.75 +/- 0.02 mm, 1 kg spool. Density 1.20 g/cm3.\nDrying: 50 C for 4 h.\nNozzle sizes: 0.2 / 0.4 / 0.6 mm - the TDS does NOT list 0.8.\nNozzle temp: 195-205 C at 50-100 mm/s; 205-220 C at 100-300 mm/s.\nBed: 50-60 C. Bed type: textured PEI sheet / cool plate.\nCooling fan: 100 %.\n\nTEMPERATURE:\nA 0.8 nozzle moves roughly four times the material per second at the same head speed, so it is read against the TDS's faster band, 205-220 C. 220 C is that band's top.\nThe parent runs a 230 C first layer. That is above anything the TDS sanctions anywhere, so it is clamped to 220 C - the whole reason a first-layer override appears in this file at all.\n\nNOT OVERRIDDEN: fan stays at the parent's 100 %, which matches the TDS. Bed 60 C is both the vendor's ceiling and the parent's value.\n\nUNTESTED - no calibration print has been run with this profile yet."
